[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":126},"en/routes/conteudo-do-cubo.tsx",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10,"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":20,"_21":22,"_23":24,"_25":26},"tipo","metodo","cubo",{"_11":124,"_13":124,"_28":125},"id","guimond","nome","Guimond","nomeLongo","Orientation, separation and PBL","termo",{"_28":121,"_122":123},"niveis",[50,75],"introducao","<p>A fast 2x2 method that first twists the corners and only then puts each one in place: white and yellow count the same until the end of orientation. It has 4 steps and ends with the same <a href=\"/en/glossary#pbl\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"On the 2x2 (Ortega): puts the pieces of both layers in place at once.\">PBL</a> as <a href=\"/en/glossary#ortega\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"A 2x2 method: it builds one face, orients the top one (Ortega OLL) and permutes both layers at once (PBL).\">Ortega</a>, so if you know Ortega you already have half of it. To start, there is a version with just 2 algorithms: <a href=\"/en/2x2/guimond/iniciante\">Guimond with 2 algorithms</a>.</p>\n","etapas",[32,33,34,35],"historias",[27],{"_13":14,"_28":29,"_30":31},"endereco","/historia#guimond","resumo","The method is by Gaétan Guimond, a cuber from Montreal, Canada, who says on his website that he created it in 1982.",{"_11":114,"_13":115,"_38":116,"_40":117,"_42":118,"_43":-7,"_45":119},{"_11":84,"_13":85,"_38":86,"_40":87,"_42":88,"_43":89,"_45":90},{"_11":64,"_13":65,"_38":66,"_40":67,"_42":68,"_43":69,"_45":70},{"_11":36,"_13":37,"_38":39,"_40":41,"_42":-7,"_43":44,"_45":46},"pbl","PBL","html","<p>The same <a href=\"/en/glossary#pbl\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"On the 2x2 (Ortega): puts the pieces of both layers in place at once.\">PBL</a> as <a href=\"/en/glossary#ortega\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"A 2x2 method: it builds one face, orients the top one (Ortega OLL) and permutes both layers at once (PBL).\">Ortega</a>: both faces are done, the corners just need swapping until the sides match.</p>\n","grupos",[47],"pagina","treino","/2x2/treino?grupo=ortega-pbl","imagem","/imagens/diagramas/02b6a512b5070e6c.svg",{"_11":48,"_13":48,"_49":50,"_51":52,"_53":54,"_55":56,"_28":57},"Ortega PBL","nivel","iniciante","casos",6,"conjunto",false,"ids",[58,59,60,61,62,63],"/2x2/ortega-pbl","2X2-PBL-Adj","2X2-PBL-Opp","2X2-PBL-OppOpp","2X2-PBL-AdjAdj","2X2-PBL-AdjOpp","2X2-PBL-OppAdj","separacao","Separation","<p>Swap corners between the layers until all the white is on the bottom and all the yellow is on top. There are 6 cases, with short algorithms (1 to 5 turns).</p>\n",[72],{"_13":65,"_28":71},"/2x2/treino?grupo=guimond-separacao","/imagens/diagramas/0f92325f9e7f2651.svg","/2x2/guimond/separacao",{"_11":73,"_13":74,"_49":75,"_51":52,"_53":54,"_55":76,"_28":77},"Guimond Separação","Guimond Separation","intermediario",[78,79,80,81,82,83],"/2x2/guimond-separacao","2X2-GS-Vizinhos-e-vizinhos","2X2-GS-Um-e-um","2X2-GS-Tres-e-tres","2X2-GS-Diagonal-e-diagonal","2X2-GS-Diagonal-em-cima","2X2-GS-Diagonal-embaixo","orientacao","Orientation","<p>Leave the top and bottom faces with only white and yellow, mixed. Turn <code>D</code> until the twisted bottom corner is at front-right, and see where its white or yellow points (front or right). Then count how many top corners already have white or yellow facing up: there are 16 cases, almost all with 3 or 4 turns. If all 4 bottom corners are already right, use an <a href=\"/en/glossary#ortega\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"A 2x2 method: it builds one face, orients the top one (Ortega OLL) and permutes both layers at once (PBL).\">Ortega</a> <a href=\"/en/glossary#oll\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Makes the top face all one color, without caring about the position of the pieces. There are 57 cases; in 2-Look OLL, 10 cases in two parts.\">OLL</a>.</p>\n",[92],{"_13":85,"_28":91},"/2x2/treino?grupo=guimond-orientacao","/imagens/diagramas/748a0d9130bfcd25.svg","/2x2/guimond/orientacao",{"_11":93,"_13":94,"_49":75,"_51":95,"_53":54,"_55":96,"_28":97},"Guimond Orientação","Guimond Orientation",16,[98,99,100,101,102,103,104,105,106,107,108,109,110,111,112,113],"/2x2/guimond-orientacao","2X2-GO-Tres-direita","2X2-GO-Tres-frente","2X2-GO-Vizinhos-frente","2X2-GO-Vizinhos-direita","2X2-GO-Diagonal-frente","2X2-GO-Diagonal-direita","2X2-GO-Um-A-direita","2X2-GO-Um-A-frente","2X2-GO-Um-B-direita","2X2-GO-Um-B-frente","2X2-GO-Um-C-direita","2X2-GO-Um-C-frente","2X2-GO-Nenhum-A-direita","2X2-GO-Nenhum-A-frente","2X2-GO-Nenhum-B-frente","2X2-GO-Nenhum-B-direita","tres-quartos","¾ of a face","<p>Three stickers on the bottom, each white or yellow (they can be mixed). It almost always takes one or two turns: plan it during <a href=\"/en/glossary#inspecao\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"The 15 seconds to look at the cube before you start solving, without turning the faces.\">inspection</a>.</p>\n",[],{"_13":115,"_28":120},"/imagens/diagramas/5e712bf63143a22e.svg","/2x2/guimond/tres-quartos","/en/glossary#guimond","dica","A 2x2 method: it twists the corners so white and yellow are on top and bottom (mixed), separates the two colors and finishes with Ortega's…","2x2","/2x2/",{"_127":128,"_129":130},"cubos",[133,134,135,136,137,138,139],"idiomas",[131,132],"pt","en",{"_11":148,"_13":148},{"_11":124,"_13":124},{"_11":147,"_13":147},{"_11":146,"_13":146},{"_11":144,"_13":145},{"_11":142,"_13":143},{"_11":140,"_13":141},"skewb","Skewb","pyraminx","Pyraminx","megaminx","Megaminx","5x5","4x4","3x3"]
